TEST 38098 -- MRP ring switch over with 200ms recovery time
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-30 15:01-15:16 NZDT, tb470, hand-driven (no framework script), queue row 9.
Tester: bench-runner. Case text: AWPTCM-T38098 (ck.db zephyr_cases), 8 steps.

VERDICT: PASS -- labelled CLEAN (8 switch-overs, copper and fibre, from both ends;
one sub-step UNSUPPORTED, one observation carried from T38093).

  Every switch-over recovered within the 200 ms profile. Worst outage per run,
  over all four flows: 94-146 ms (8 of 8 runs; median ~105 ms). After each
  shutdown the MRM unblocked its blocked ring port, reported Network Status Open,
  and traffic continued on the other link. No duplicates and no echoes occurred
  during any switch-over.
  UNSUPPORTED (step 8, "Fixed ports"): the IE520-28GSX has no fixed copper port;
  every front port is an SFP/SFP+ cage (orient-dt §2). The SFP/SFP+ legs were
  measured: copper = AT-SP10TM (10GBASE-TM SFP+, linked at 1000) and
  fibre = AT-SPSX (1000BASE-SX).
  OBSERVATION (not a step of this case; T38093's FAIL): each link RESTORE, i.e.
  each ring closure, looped VLAN 1 for 31-62 ms on 8 of 8 runs. The mechanism is
  the MRM's false TestTimerExpired -> "Ring opened". The unicast hole during those
  restores was up to 180 ms. This case has no restore step and is not graded on
  the restores; see 38093-fail.log.

